  "user_handle": "0xdice91",
  "body": "## Finding description and impact\nIn CLOB.sol the functions [_processLimitBidOrder](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-07-gte-clob/blob/92a8839e3eb9715d53e24f0168442cecdc9b784b/contracts/clob/CLOB.sol#L503) and [_processLimitAskOrder](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-07-gte-clob/blob/92a8839e3eb9715d53e24f0168442cecdc9b784b/contracts/clob/CLOB.sol#L544) are used to process buy and sell limit orders, respectively, these functions execute the order to return the `quoteTokenAmount` and `baseTokenAmount`.These amounts represent the amounts sent in or received, depending on the kind of order.\n```solidity\n    /// @dev Places a bid limit order onto the book, matching and settling any fill if possible\n    function _processLimitBidOrder(\n        Book storage ds,\n        address account,\n        Order memory newOrder,\n        PostLimitOrderArgs memory args\n    ) internal returns (PostLimitOrderResult memory) {\n        (uint256 postAmount, uint256 quoteTokenAmountSent, uint256 baseTokenAmountReceived) =\n            _executeBidLimitOrder(ds, newOrder, args.limitOrderType);\n\n\n        if (postAmount + quoteTokenAmountSent + baseTokenAmountReceived == 0) revert ZeroOrder();\n\n\n@>       if (baseTokenAmountReceived != quoteTokenAmountSent && baseTokenAmountReceived & quoteTokenAmountSent == 0) {\n            revert ZeroCostTrade();\n        }\n//More code...\n}\n\n\n    /// @dev Places an ask limit order onto the book, matching and settling any fill if possible\n    function _processLimitAskOrder(\n        Book storage ds,\n        address account,\n        Order memory newOrder,\n        PostLimitOrderArgs memory args\n    ) internal returns (PostLimitOrderResult memory) {\n        (uint256 postAmount, uint256 quoteTokenAmountReceived, uint256 baseTokenAmountSent) =\n            _executeAskLimitOrder(ds, newOrder, args.limitOrderType);\n\n\n        if (postAmount + quoteTokenAmountReceived + baseTokenAmountSent == 0) revert ZeroOrder();\n\n\n@>      if (baseTokenAmountSent != quoteTokenAmountReceived && baseTokenAmountSent & quoteTokenAmountReceived == 0) {\n            revert ZeroCostTrade();\n        }\n\n//More code...\n}\n\n\n```\nThese function have a check meant to ensure that these values (`baseTokenAmountReceived` and `quoteTokenAmountSent`) are either both equal (or zero) or if one is of them is greater than zero,then the other can never be zero.\n```solidity\n if (baseTokenAmountReceived != quoteTokenAmountSent && baseTokenAmountReceived & quoteTokenAmountSent == 0) {\n            revert ZeroCostTrade();\n        }\n```\nThe `issue` here is based on ` bitwise disjointness`. \nThese functions use the bitwise AND operator. The AND operation under the hood simply compares each bit of two numbers, bit-by-bit, and returns 1 only if `both` bits are 1, or zero otherwise.\n```\n1 & 1 = 1\n1 & 0 = 0\n0 & 1 = 0\n0 & 0 = 0\n```\nBitwise disjointness results from the fact that two numbers A and B will produce A & B == 0 if and only if they have no overlapping 1 bits.\nTherefore, in a situation where the resultant `baseTokenAmountReceived` and `quoteTokenAmountSent` are  bitwise disjointed values, that is in each value the bits are in such a way that there is `no` position in which there is 1 in both values at the same time. \n```\nA = 1100 -> 12\nB = 0011 -> 3\n---------\n    0000  → This is zero\n\n\nA = 0b01010100  // 84\nB = 0b10101011  // 171\nA & B = 0b00000000  // = 0\n\n//for larger values\nA = 147573952589676412928\nB = 295147905179352825856\nA & B = 0b0000000000000000  // = 0\n\n\nA = 1152921504606846976  //1e18 value -> like WETH\nB = 456373836            //1e6 value  -> like USDC\nA & B = 0b00000000000000  // = 0\n\n```\nThere are lots of numbers that can occur during conversion, in which their bits align in such a way that their AND will give zero, despite these values being perfectly valid, resulting in wrong reverts of the limit order\nSince the `quotetoken` and `basetoken` may be of different decimals in the order book, the conversion can happen at any price provided by the makers or takers. \n\nAny limit order being placed which gets filled partially, which results in `baseTokenAmountReceived` and `quoteTokenAmountSent` that are bitwise disjoint values, although perfectly normal, will revert due to their AND returning zero.\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nThe check should be rewritten using || and avoid the AND operator. Although this may be less gas efficient, but will prevent this case from happening.",
  "proof_of_concept": "```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity ^0.8.0;\n\nimport {PoCTestBase} from \"./PoCTestBase.t.sol\";\nimport {console} from \"forge-std/console.sol\";\nimport \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\n\ncontract PoC is PoCTestBase {\n    error ZeroCostTrade();\n    error ZeroOrder();\n   \n    function test_submissionValidity() external {\n\n        Mocklimitprocessor limitprocessor = new Mocklimitprocessor();\n\n\n        // lets say the base amount of 1152921504606846976 //1.15e18\n        // and a price of 395878010 \n        // the quote amount will be 1152921504606846976 * 395878010 / 1e18 = 456.5e6  \n        //but thier AND will give 0 in the check reverting the order\n\n       vm.expectRevert(ZeroCostTrade.selector);\n       limitprocessor.mock_processLimitBidOrder(1152921504606846976, 395878010, 0);\n            \n    }\n\n}\n\ncontract Mocklimitprocessor {\n\n    error ZeroCostTrade();\n    error ZeroOrder();\n\n\n    function mock_processLimitBidOrder( \n       uint256 baseTokenAmountReceived,\n        uint256 price,\n        uint256 postAmount\n    ) external returns (uint256 quoteTokenAmountSent) {\n       \n        quoteTokenAmountSent = getQuoteTokenAmount(price, baseTokenAmountReceived);\n        console.log(quoteTokenAmountSent);\n\n        if (postAmount + quoteTokenAmountSent + baseTokenAmountReceived == 0) revert ZeroOrder();\n\n        if (baseTokenAmountReceived != quoteTokenAmountSent && baseTokenAmountReceived & quoteTokenAmountSent == 0) {\n            revert ZeroCostTrade();\n         } \n        \n        return quoteTokenAmountSent;\n    \n       \n    }\n\n    function getQuoteTokenAmount(uint256 price, uint256 baseAmount)\n        internal\n        view\n        returns (uint256 quoteAmount)\n    {   //self.config().baseSize = 1e18 as the base token is 18 decimals\n        return baseAmount * price / 1e18;\n    }\n\n\n}\n\n```",
